263	<!-- Q1 -->
264	<div class="question-block" id="q1">
265	  <div class="q-num">Question 1</div>
266	  <div class="q-text">What does the <code>PYBIND11_MODULE(oil_volume_cpp, m)</code> macro expand to under the hood?</div>
267	  <div class="options">
268	    <button class="option-btn" onclick="answer('q1',0,false)"><span class="option-key">A</span>A Python class definition that registers the module in <code>sys.modules</code></button>
269	    <button class="option-btn" onclick="answer('q1',1,true)"><span class="option-key">B</span>An <code>extern "C"</code> function named <code>PyInit_oil_volume_cpp</code> that Python's import machinery calls when loading the shared library</button>
270	    <button class="option-btn" onclick="answer('q1',2,false)"><span class="option-key">C</span>A code-generation step that emits a <code>.py</code> wrapper file alongside the <code>.so</code></button>
271	    <button class="option-btn" onclick="answer('q1',3,false)"><span class="option-key">D</span>A linker script that merges the C++ object file with <code>libpython</code></button>
272	  </div>
273	  <div class="feedback correct" id="q1-fb-correct">Correct. The macro emits <code>extern "C" PyObject* PyInit_oil_volume_cpp()</code> — the exact symbol Python's import system looks for when it <code>dlopen()</code>s the shared library. The name must exactly match the module name.</div>
274	  <div class="feedback wrong"   id="q1-fb-wrong">Not quite. The macro expands to <code>extern "C" PyObject* PyInit_oil_volume_cpp()</code> — an entry-point function Python's loader calls after <code>dlopen()</code>. No code generation, no class, no linker script.</div>
275	</div>
