362	<div class="question-block" id="q8">
363	  <div class="q-num">Question 8</div>
364	  <div class="q-text">What does the ABI tag in the filename <code>oil_volume_cpp.cpython-312-x86_64-linux-gnu.so</code> indicate?</div>
365	  <div class="options">
366	    <button class="option-btn" onclick="answer('q8',0,false)"><span class="option-key">A</span>The extension was compiled with GCC 3.12 and requires that exact compiler version to load</button>
367	    <button class="option-btn" onclick="answer('q8',1,false)"><span class="option-key">B</span>The extension uses the Python Limited API and is compatible with all Python versions from 3.12 onward</button>
368	    <button class="option-btn" onclick="answer('q8',2,true)"><span class="option-key">C</span>The extension was compiled for CPython 3.12 on x86-64 Linux and is not binary-compatible with other Python versions, architectures, or implementations</button>
369	    <button class="option-btn" onclick="answer('q8',3,false)"><span class="option-key">D</span>The extension requires GLIBC 3.12 or newer</button>
370	  </div>
371	  <div class="feedback correct" id="q8-fb-correct">Correct. The cpython-312 tag means it was compiled against CPython 3.12's C API. If you upgrade to Python 3.13, you must recompile. The platform tag (x86_64-linux-gnu) means it will not run on ARM or Windows.</div>
372	  <div class="feedback wrong"   id="q8-fb-wrong">The ABI tag encodes the Python implementation (cpython), version (3.12), architecture (x86_64), and OS (linux-gnu). The <code>.so</code> is binary-incompatible with Python 3.11, 3.13, ARM, or PyPy without recompilation.</div>
373	</div>
